		<chapter num="17">
			<heading>
				Proverbs 17
			</heading>
			<begin-paragraph>
			</begin-paragraph>
			<v n="1">than a house full of feasting with strife .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017002">
			</marker>
			<v n="2">and<crossref let="o" cid="c20017002.2" />will share the inheritance as one of the brothers .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017003">
			</marker>
			<v n="3">
				<crossref let="q" cid="c20017003.2" />and the Lord tests hearts .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017004">
			</marker>
			<v n="4">and a liar gives ear to a mischievous tongue .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017005">
			</marker>
			<v n="5">he who is<crossref let="s" cid="c20017005.2" />glad at calamity will not go<crossref let="t" cid="c20017005.3" />unpunished .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017006">
			</marker>
			<v n="6">and the glory of children is their fathers .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017007">
			</marker>
			<v n="7">still less is<crossref let="x" cid="c20017007.2" />false speech to a prince .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017008">
			</marker>
			<v n="8">wherever he turns he prospers .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017009">
			</marker>
			<v n="9">but he who repeats a matter<crossref let="a" cid="c20017009.1" />separates close friends .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017010">
			</marker>
			<v n="10">than a hundred blows into a fool .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017011">
			</marker>
			<v n="11">and<crossref let="b" cid="c20017011.1" />a cruel messenger will be sent against him .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017012">
			</marker>
			<v n="12">
				<crossref let="d" cid="c20017012.2" />rather than a fool in his folly .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017013">
			</marker>
			<v n="13">
				<crossref let="f" cid="c20017013.2" />evil will not depart from his house .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017014">
			</marker>
			<v n="14">so<crossref let="g" cid="c20017014.1" />quit before the quarrel breaks out .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017015">
			</marker>
			<v n="15">are both alike an abomination to the Lord .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017016">
			</marker>
			<v n="16">when he has no sense ?</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017017">
			</marker>
			<v n="17">and a brother is born for adversity .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017018">
			</marker>
			<v n="18">and puts up security in the presence of his neighbor .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017019">
			</marker>
			<v n="19">he who<crossref let="l" cid="c20017019.1" />makes his door high seeks destruction .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017020">
			</marker>
			<v n="20">and one with a dishonest tongue falls into calamity .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017021">
			</marker>
			<v n="21">and the father of a fool has no joy .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017022">
			</marker>
			<v n="22">but a crushed spirit<crossref let="p" cid="c20017022.2" />dries up the bones .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017023">
			</marker>
			<v n="23">to<crossref let="r" cid="c20017023.2" />pervert the ways of justice .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017024">
			</marker>
			<v n="24">but the eyes of a fool are on the ends of the earth .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017025">
			</marker>
			<v n="25">
				<crossref let="t" cid="c20017025.2" />and bitterness to<crossref let="u" cid="c20017025.3" />her who bore him .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017026">
			</marker>
			<v n="26">nor to strike the noble for their uprightness .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017027">
			</marker>
			<v n="27">and he who has a cool spirit is a man of understanding .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017028">
			</marker>
			<v n="28">when he closes his lips , he is deemed intelligent .</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v20017029">
			</marker>
